+# Feature Specification: Task ids
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-20 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Give each task a unique identifier that still works after the task is renamed.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Refer to a task by a stable id (Priority: P1)
+Each added task carries an `id`, unique in its list, that never changes (rename included).
+
+**Independent Test**: add two tasks, ids differ; rename one, id unchanged.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** an empty list, **When** two tasks are added, **Then** each has a string `id` and the ids differ.
+2. **Given** a task, **When** it is renamed, completed, tagged, **Then** its id is unchanged.
+3. **Given** a removed task, **When** another is added, **Then** the new id differs from every id handed out before.
+
+### User Story 2 - Look up and act by id (Priority: P1)
+`get(id)` returns the task as a Result; `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`, `remove` accept an id as well as a title.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** a task, **When** `get(id)` is called, **Then** the task is returned.
+2. **Given** an unknown id, **When** `get` is called, **Then** a `not-found` error is returned.
+3. **Given** a renamed task, **When** acted on by its id, **Then** the action works.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- A title equal to another task's id: the id wins.
+- `get` accepts ids only, not titles.
+- Renaming by id to a title already used by another task is still a `duplicate` error.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: Every task has a string `id`, unique among all tasks ever added to the list (removed ids are not reused).
+- **FR-002**: A task's id never changes.
+- **FR-003**: `get(id)` returns `Result<Task>`; unknown id gives `not-found`.
+- **FR-004**: The seven title methods accept a title or an id; an id match takes precedence over a title match.
+- **FR-005**: Ids are generated without clock or randomness (constitution).
+
+## Success Criteria
+- SC-001: Any task can be reached by id after any number of renames.
+- SC-002: No two tasks added to one list share an id.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Id format is opaque; ids are per list, not global across lists.
